    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d381">

                <pb facs="0407" n="403" sameAs="frus:frus1939v03/pg403"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.516/600: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Peck</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-05-10T17:00:00+07:00">May 10, 1939—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 10—1:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>323. Reference Department’s telegram No. 143, May 4, 1 p.m.; and my telegram No.
                    320, May 10, 2 p.m.<anchor n="49" xml:id="d381-f1"/> The Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs this morning orally expressed to me the hope of the Chinese <pb
                        facs="0408" n="404" xml:id="pg404"/> Government that American banks would do
                    nothing that would assist the newly formed Huahsing Bank in Shanghai which he
                    said had been created by the Japanese as a means of attacking Chinese
                    currency.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Peiping, Shanghai.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peck</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
